    "text": "The committed data do not show GEODE cheaper than Meep for this forward solve. At the one rung with a GEODE cost, Meep R2.5 reaches the same error against Palace p3 in 0.63x the time and 0.09x the memory, and returns the whole spectrum. Against the extrapolated reference neither solver is within the reference uncertainty. The title hypothesis (FEM cheaper by a moderate factor) is therefore not supported on this evidence, but it is not decided: GEODE has one cost rung, Meep has two non-monotone resolutions, and the optimized-geometry pair and the optimizer comparison are open."
